      "note": "âš âš  THE ONE THAT CATCHES A LANGUAGE'S DEFAULT SORT. U+1D11E is F0 9D 84 9E in UTF-8 but the surrogate pair D834 DD1E in UTF-16. U+FFFF is EF BF BF in UTF-8 and FFFF in UTF-16. So UTF-8 puts U+FFFF FIRST and UTF-16 puts it SECOND â€” opposite orders. Neither language's default sort is safe; both must be told to compare UTF-8 bytes."
